    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "George & Maguire Properties are delighted to present No. 12A Fernley Court, an attractive two-storey, mid-terrace townhouse discreetly positioned within a small enclave off Long Lane in the heart of Dublin 8.\r\nExtending to approximately 65 sq. m / 700 sq. ft, the well-proportioned accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall with guest WC, leading to a bright and spacious dual-aspect kitchen/living/dining room, together with useful storage. Upstairs, there are two double bedrooms, an en suite and a family bathroom. Outside, the development offers a well-maintained communal area with landscaped flower beds, refuse facilities and bicycle storage.\r\nA particularly valuable feature is the secure designated underground parking space—an increasingly rare benefit for a property situated this close to Dublin city centre.\r\nThe location is exceptional, with the peaceful surroundings of St Kevin's Park just moments away and Camden Street within a two-minute walk. An excellent selection of cafés, restaurants and bars is nearby, including Mister S, Pickle, Hang Dai, Sprezzatura, Delahunt, Uno Mas and Network Café. St Stephen's Green, Grafton Street and the city centre are also within comfortable walking distance.\r\nThe property is convenient to Griffith College, Trinity College Dublin and several well-regarded primary and secondary schools, as well as many of Dublin's principal places of business. No. 12A is likely to appeal to first-time buyers, downsizers and investors seeking a private and highly convenient city home with the added advantage of secure underground parking.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall: Laminate timber flooring, leading to the open-plan kitchen/living/dining room.\r\nGuest WC: Tiled flooring, WC and WHB.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Living/Dining Room: Bright and spacious dual-aspect room with solid timber wall and floor kitchen units, an integrated oven and hob, stainless-steel sink and tiled splashback. Feature box-bay window overlooking the private rear courtyard.\r\n\r\nLanding: Providing access to both bedrooms and the family bathroom.\r\n\r\nBedroom One: Double room overlooking the private rear courtyard, with fitted wardrobes.\r\n\r\nEn Suite: Timber flooring, WC, WHB and fully tiled shower cubicle.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom: Timber flooring, WC, WHB and bath with tiled surround, glazed screen and shower attachment.\r\n\r\nManagement Charge: €1,450 per annum\r\nSecure designated underground parking space\r\nAttractive two-storey townhouse extending to approximately 65 sq. m / 700sq. ft\r\nBright and spacious dual-aspect kitchen/living/dining room\r\nTwo double bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with en suite\r\nGuest WC at entrance level\r\nQuietly positioned within a small, private enclave\r\nSt Kevin's Park just moments away\r\nCamden Street within a two-minute walk"
      },
